              "sourceRegion": "Question 3(a), upper right column",
              "description": "A 3 by 3 unit grid containing a triangle with vertices (0,1), (2,0), (3,3). Coordinates are reconstruction data and are not printed. A blank-grid template cannot express the supplied triangle.",
              "mathematics": "Enclosing area 9; complementary triangle areas 3, 1 and 3/2.",
              "answerVisibility": "Only the supplied grid and triangle are visible."
            },
            "derived": false,
            "reviewStatus": "needs-review"
          }
        ],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$3.5$ square units.",
          "worked": "Subtract the three complementary triangle areas from the square.\n$$\\begin{align*}A&=3\\times3-\\frac{3\\times2}{2}-\\frac{2\\times1}{2}-\\frac{1\\times3}{2}\\\\A&=9-3-1-\\frac32\\\\A&=3.5\\text{ square units}.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
